{
  "name": "02 - Credit Report Ingestion",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 02 \u2014 Credit Report Ingestion (pluggable)\n\nOne workflow, three interchangeable data-source adapters. The `credit_data_source` field on the case decides which path runs:\n\n- **crs_api** \u2014 CRS Credit API, a licensed reseller for all three bureaus. Consumer authenticates directly; no passwords stored. **Recommended.**\n- **pdf_upload** \u2014 the client uploads their own report; we parse it.\n- **identityiq** \u2014 adapter for an IdentityIQ session.\n\nAll three normalize into one standard schema downstream.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "888534d3-419b-4972-8057-61d3e3f48685",
      "name": "Note 89a6a430",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Legal note on the IdentityIQ adapter\n\nStoring a customer's IdentityIQ password and logging in on their behalf violates IdentityIQ's Terms of Service and creates real security liability. This adapter calls an **external RPA / browser-automation service** that the *customer* drives \u2014 it should never hold raw third-party passwords in n8n. Prefer `crs_api` or `pdf_upload`. Keep this path disabled until reviewed by counsel.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "dd937a67-1b9b-426d-bb3b-5001899148d3",
      "name": "Note 7e7a5372",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      },
      "id": "d4794650-6d97-403a-8b4b-bab4a5d7038b",
      "name": "When Called by Orchestrator",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT case_id, first_name, last_name, date_of_birth, ssn_last4,\n       street, city, state, zip, credit_data_source\nFROM cases WHERE case_id = $1;",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "039fd663-399d-4b34-a113-c95a2fa53781",
      "name": "DB: Load Case",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
